course: dictionary
lesson: 13425
title: Holiness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Holiness is a noun. It means the quality of being holy: very good and connected with God or a religion. Like other words for qualities, it names something you can notice but cannot touch.
explain: The clues around the word show its meaning. «The silent temple was filled with a deep holiness that made everyone speak softly.» The silence and the soft speaking tell you that people feel great respect for the place.
explain: Holiness also appears in a title. «His Holiness the Pope visited the city.» Here the words are a polite way of addressing a religious leader. The capital letters show it is a title, not a description of how good he is.
fact: Holiness means the quality of being holy.
fact: Holy means very good and connected with God or a religion.
fact: Holiness is uncountable, so you talk about «much holiness» or «a sense of holiness», not «a holiness» in the quality sense.
fact: «His Holiness» is a polite title for some religious leaders, such as the Pope or the Dalai Lama.
fact: A capital letter in «His Holiness» shows it is a title, while lowercase holiness names a quality.
exercise: «The monk was known for his holiness and kindness.» What does holiness mean here? | Being rich and famous | Being very tall and strong | * Being very good and connected with God or a religion | Being lost and tired
exercise: «His Holiness the Pope visited the city.» In this sentence, what is «His Holiness»? | A type of church bell | * A polite title for a religious leader | The name of a city | A friendly dog
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the quality of being holy. «The temple was quiet, and the holiness of the place made people speak softly.» | softly | * holiness | temple | quiet
test: Why is «His Holiness» written with capital letters? | It is the start of a question | It is the name of a town | * It is a title used to address a religious leader politely | It shows the speaker is shouting
test: Which sentence uses holiness as a quality, not as a title? | «Holiness is a title for the Pope.» | «His Holiness the Dalai Lama smiled.» | «His Holiness spoke to the crowd.» | * «The pilgrims felt holiness in the quiet cathedral.»
exam: In the sentence «The old chapel had a calm holiness», what does holiness mean? | Noisy and busy | Cold and wet | Money and wealth | * A deep, religious goodness that deserves respect
